# Static Site Architecture

Convert from server-rendered Hono app to pre-compiled static site.

## Architecture Overview

```
Before:                    After:
┌─────────────┐           ┌─────────────┐
│  Hono/JSX   │           │  Static HTML  │
│  (server)   │    →      │  (prebuilt)   │
│  HTMX       │           │  Vanilla JS   │
│  API routes │           │  (no build)   │
└─────────────┘           └─────────────┘
```

## Key Changes

### 1. Build-Time Rendering
- Pre-render all JSX components to static HTML at build time
- No server-side rendering at runtime
- Use a build tool (Vite) to compile JSX → HTML

### 2. Client-Side Logic
- Move all interactivity to vanilla JavaScript
- Replace HTMX with plain JS event handlers
- No backend API calls (all client-side or use edge functions)

### 3. LLM API Handling
**Challenge**: Can't expose API keys in client-side code

**Options**:
1. **User-provided API key** - Store in localStorage, user enters their own
2. **Proxy edge function** - Lightweight Cloudflare function (not full backend)
3. **Remove LLM** - Make it a static chat UI only

**Recommended**: Option 1 for simplicity - static site with user-managed keys

## File Structure

```
src/
  pages/           # Page components (build to HTML)
    index.tsx
    privacy.tsx
  components/      # Reusable components
    ChatBox.tsx
    Message.tsx
    ...
  lib/             # Utilities (ES5 compatible)
    storage.ts     # localStorage wrapper
    llm-client.ts  # Client-side LLM API
    dom.ts         # DOM manipulation helpers
  tests/           # Test files
public/            # Static assets
dist/              # Build output (deploy this)
```

## Build Configuration

- Use Vite with `@vitejs/plugin-legacy` for ES5 output
- Target: IE11 / Kindle Browser compatibility
- Output: Static HTML + bundled JS

## Component Patterns

```typescript
// ❌ BAD - Server component with HTMX
export const ChatBox = () => (
  <form hx-post="/chat">...</form>
);

// ✅ GOOD - Static component with client hydration
export function ChatBox() {
  // Return HTML string or DOM element
  return '<form id="chat-form">...</form>';
}

// ✅ GOOD - Client-side initialization
function initChatBox() {
  var form = document.getElementById('chat-form');
  form.onsubmit = function(e) {
    e.preventDefault();
    handleSubmit(form);
  };
}

// Initialize when DOM is ready
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', initChatBox);
```

## State Management

Use simple patterns compatible with old browsers:
```typescript
// Global state object (simple module pattern)
var AppState = {
  messages: [],
  apiKey: localStorage.getItem('apiKey') || ''
};

// Update and persist
function addMessage(msg) {
  AppState.messages.push(msg);
  renderMessages();
}
```

## Deployment

- Build: `npm run build` → outputs to `dist/`
- Deploy `dist/` to any static host (GitHub Pages, Cloudflare Pages, etc.)
- No server runtime required
